  "base_commit": "ab746bce666a117c6570dc129602125c6c859818",
  "pr_number": 5448,
  "issue_number": 5239,
  "issue_title": "fix: Raycast Create Install/Config Snippet actions never render (feed omits the fields the check depends on)",
  "issue_body": "## Goal\nFix the Raycast extension's \"Create Install Snippet\"/\"Create Config Snippet\" actions (and the \"Copy Install Command\"/\"Copy Config\" actions in Trending/Recent Updates) so they actually appear for entries that have an install command or config snippet, instead of never rendering at all.\n\n## Why this matters\nThis is a live, reproducible bug in the shipped Raycast extension, not a hypothetical. The feed generator only puts a compact subset of fields (`installable`, `hasInstallCommand`, `hasConfigSnippet`, `mcpInstallTargets`) into the cached/fetched `raycast-index.json` feed \u2014 the actual `installCommand`/`configSnippet` text only exists in the per-entry detail payload. But the client code that decides whether to show these actions reads `entry.installCommand`/`entry.configSnippet` directly off the feed entry, which is always an empty string, so the check always evaluates false.\n\n## Current behavior\n`buildCompactInstallFields()` (`packages/registry/src/artifacts-lib.js:552-568`, used by `buildRaycastEntries`, lines 898-924) never includes the raw `installCommand`/`configSnippet` text in feed entries. The client's `normalizeRaycastEntry` (`integrations/raycast/src/feed.ts:621-622`) sets `installCommand`/`configSnippet` via `optionalRawString(value.installCommand)`, which returns `\"\"` when the field is `undefined` (`integrations/raycast/src/utils.ts:11-13`) \u2014 so every feed-loaded entry has `entry.installCommand === \"\"` and `entry.configSnippet === \"\"` regardless of whether the real entry has one.\n\nTwo consumers are broken by this:\n- `integrations/raycast/src/discovery-command.tsx:389-390` (used by both `trending.tsx` and `recent-updates.tsx`) computes `hasInstallCommand = Boolean(entry.installCommand.trim())` / `hasConfig = Boolean(entry.configSnippet.trim())` \u2014 always `false`, so \"Copy Install Command\", \"Copy Config\", \"Create Install Snippet\", and \"Create Config Snippet\" (lines 430-513) never render in Trending or Recent Updates, for any entry.\n- `integrations/raycast/src/registry-command.tsx:1110,1120` (used by `search.tsx` and every `search-*.tsx` command) gates `Action.CreateSnippet` for install/config directly on `entry.installCommand.trim()`/`entry.configSnippet.trim()` \u2014 same bug, so these two actions never appear in any of the 11 search commands.\n\nNotably, the same file (`registry-command.tsx`) already has the correct pattern elsewhere: its \"Use\" / copy-to-clipboard section (lines 683-706, 941-944) correctly checks `entry.hasInstallCommand`/`entry.hasConfigSnippet` and fetches the detail payload via `loadEntryDetail` before copying \u2014 proving the right approach is already known and used in the same file, just not applied to the \"Create Snippet\" actions.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\"Create Install Snippet\"/\"Create Config Snippet\" (and Trending/Recent Updates' \"Copy Install Command\"/\"Copy Config\") gate on the boolean feed fields (`entry.hasInstallCommand`/`entry.hasConfigSnippet`) and fetch the entry detail payload (matching the existing `loadEntryDetail` pattern) before building the snippet/copy text, for any entry that actually has one.\n\n## Scope\n- integrations/raycast/src/discovery-command.tsx\n- integrations/raycast/src/registry-command.tsx\n\n## Out of scope\n- packages/registry/src/artifacts-lib.js's buildCompactInstallFields/buildRaycastEntries (an alternative fix would be adding the raw text to the compact feed, but that increases feed payload size for every entry; prefer the detail-fetch approach used elsewhere in the same file unless a maintainer prefers the feed-size tradeoff)\n- Any other Raycast command not named above\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- PR includes `Closes #<issue>`.\n- \"Create Install Snippet\"/\"Create Config Snippet\" actions appear in search commands for entries with hasInstallCommand/hasConfigSnippet true, and are absent for entries without.\n- \"Copy Install Command\"/\"Copy Config\" actions appear in Trending/Recent Updates under the same condition.\n- The fix follows the existing loadEntryDetail pattern already used for copy-to-clipboard actions in the same files.\n\n## Quality evidence required in the PR\n- New features must list changed routes/components/endpoints/tools, expected behavior, and important edge cases \u2014 specifically confirm behavior for an entry with only an install command (no config), only a config (no install command), and neither.\n- No visual impact on the website; include a screen recording or screenshot of the Raycast extension showing the actions now appearing, since this is a Raycast-extension UI fix.\n\n## Validation\npnpm exec vitest run tests/raycast-entry-filters.test.ts tests/raycast-feed-detail-helpers.test.ts\ncd integrations/raycast && npm test && npm run build\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-22T21:00:27.000Z",
